    "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe M=1 FP8 GEMV (`sm120_fp8_gemv`) leaves bandwidth unused on small projections such as Qwen3.8-27B's `out` (5120x6144), which runs 64x per decode step.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`_config` now takes `k`. When N <= 6144 and K <= 6144, it uses 4 rows per warp `(4, 1, 8)` instead of `(1, 1, 8)`. Larger shapes keep their current config.\n\nThe rule covers both N and K because the win does not hold past that region: N=7168 and N=8192 lose 6-7% with 4 rows per warp, and K >= 12288 is neutral.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nMax relative error vs an fp32 reference through the public `sm120_fp8_gemv` is <= 2.9e-3 on all tested shapes, the same as before the change.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nTiming is `marker.do_bench` graph replay with the weights cloned per iteration, median, min over interleaved passes.\n\n| N x K | speedup `(4,1,8)` vs `(1,1,8)` |\n|---|---|\n| 4096 x 4096 | 1.04x |\n| 5120 x 5120 | 1.15x |\n| 5120 x 6144 (Qwen3.8-27B out) | 1.12x |\n| 6144 x 4096 | 1.07x |\n| 7168 x 5120 (unchanged) | 1.00x |\n| 16384 x 5120 (unchanged) | 1.00x |\n\nNot yet measured on RTX 5090 / RTX PRO 6000; an A/B there is needed before relying on it.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (perf-only config change; existing `test_sm120_fp8_linear.py` covers correctness)\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38818525293](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38818525293)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38818525324](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38818525324)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38818525180](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38818525180)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
